  "details": "Some of the avatars i make do not qualify as humanoids but have humanoid parts, and due to that, i have to keep making a invisible unbinded humanoid rig with extra bones for the unique parts. It is annoying and not really effective, prone to problems.\n\nMake a GameObject that can IK bind a bone transform to a default IK found on humanoids. \n\nExample: I made an non-humanoid avatar that has a head. With that new GameObject, i could bind the default head IK to what is the head in my avatar, and therefore, it will follow the rotation of my camera, making it easier for players get where i am looking. \n\nThis example above, is one of many uses there could be. It would open a new door for interesting avatar behavior.",
